[dispatch omitted 1820400 characters from the middle of this stream]

positive definite; continuity on the unit sphere in $T_x^*M$ gives $\sigma_2(\Delta)_x(\xi)\ge c_x|\xi|^2I$ for some $c_x>0$. Thus the multiplier has Gaussian decay, and Fourier inversion gives $\int_{T_xM}k_{x,1}(w,0)\,dw=I_{E_x^\bullet}$. Its graded fiber trace after composition with $\rho_g$ is $\sum_j(-1)^j\operatorname{tr}(\rho_g|_{E_x^j})$. For $n=0$, the tangent integral and determinant are both the empty-dimensional values $1$, so the same expression holds. Summing the finitely many contributions proves the stated limit conditional on [A1]. [A1, step 2.1, algebra] ∎
+
+## Proof references
+
+[Zelin Yi, §§2–5: relative tangent groupoid, rescaled heat kernels, and the Fourier-normalized fixed-point calculation](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2003.00955)
+
+[J. L. Heitsch, §3 proof of Theorem 3.1: heat trace and local Gaussian concentration, with the final local calculation abbreviated](https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~heitsch/HeitschBC.pdf)
